Altar dancing can generate large numbers of spellbooks and the
ones generated take into account your spell schools - You
usually get books in schools you know first, other schools
after those.  The process - It tries XP times to randomly give
you a book that you don't already know in a school you know,
then gives you a completely random book if that loop failed to
give you a book.  This mostly starts out giving you the books
you want the most then mixing in progressively more random
ones as you know more and more of the spells in your own
schools.  Fun gotcha - Fail to read your first blank spellbook
and blank remains an unknown book so you end up getting
lots of them but read one and you go back to getting new types
more.



